  "problem": "A restaurant manager records the total time $20$ customers waited before they were seated. The results are presented in the table below. \n\n| Waiting time (minutes) | Frequency |\n| --- | --- |\n| $0\\le x<10$ | $4$ |\n| $10\\le x<15$ | $6$ |\n| $15\\le x<20$ | $7$ |\n| $20\\le x<30$ | $3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nAssuming that the waiting times within each class interval are uniformly distributed, find an estimate of the mean waiting time $\\overset{―}{x},$ rounded to **one decimal place**.\n\nRounded to one decimal place, $\\overset{―}{x}≈$\n{{field-1}} minutes.",
